                "reply_count": 12,
                "retweet_count": 4,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Colorado is receiving $200 million through the Rural Health Transformation Program\u2014an important investment in keeping health care accessible in rural communities across our state.\n\nThis funding was included in the Working Families Tax Cuts legislation, which I voted for, to deliver long-term support for rural health systems.\n\nIt will help strengthen rural hospitals, improve care coordination, and support practical reforms that lower costs and stabilize access to care\u2014especially in districts like mine, where losing a hospital might mean the difference of life and death.\n\nRural health care in Colorado faces real pressure: workforce shortages, long travel distances, and poor lack of medical resources. This funding won\u2019t solve everything, but it moves us in the right direction. We need healthcare that\u2019s closer to home, with systems that work for rural patients and providers \n\nI\u2019ll stay focused on ensuring this program is implemented with accountability and flexibility so it delivers real results for rural Colorado. #CO03\n\nhttps://t.co/RSVY4VcxTM",
